From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Plugin: drop an unused local in s_updateEpMld

The pristine source declares chanSpec in s_updateEpMld without using it,
which prevents compiling wifiGen_fsm.c with -Wall -Wextra -Werror:

  Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c:1697:20: error: unused variable 'chanSpec' [-Werror=unused-variable]

Remove the unused declaration independently of hostapd recovery.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
index 9ca41b161e05..08356dd5f36f 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
@@ -1823,7 +1823,6 @@ static void s_updateEpMld(T_EndPoint* pEP, wld_nl80211_ifaceInfo_t* epIfInfo) {
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pRad, , ME, "NULL");
 
     int32_t linkId = NO_LINK_ID;
-    swl_chanspec_t chanSpec;
     if(epIfInfo->nMloLinks > 0) {
         swl_freqBandExt_e band = pRad->operatingFrequencyBand;
         if(band >= SWL_FREQ_BAND_EXT_NONE) {
-- 
2.55.0
